      "text": "### Overview of *People We Meet on Vacation*\n\n1. **Publisher, Release Date, and Series Status**:\n   - **Publisher**: Berkley\n   - **Release Date**: May 11, 2021\n   - **Status**: Standalone\n\n2. **Spoiler-Free Summary**:\n   *People We Meet on Vacation* follows the story of Alex and Poppy, who have been best friends for a decade and have taken annual vacations together. The narrative employs a dual-timeline structure alternating between the present day and events from two years prior, examining how their friendship deteriorated and whether it can be repaired. The book is noted for its witty banter, rich emotional stakes, and themes of friendship evolving into romance, self-discovery, and second chances.\n\n3. **Critical Reviews and Reader Reception**:\n   The novel has received praise for its engaging relationship dynamics and adept handling of themes such as friendship and romance. Reviewers have highlighted its clever dual timeline as a significant aspect that enhances the storytelling. On platforms like Goodreads, it holds a rating of approximately 3.99 out of 5 from around 640,000 ratings, indicating a strong positive reception among readers.\n\n4. **Emily Henry's Bibliography**:\n   Emily Henry is a New York Times bestselling author known for her romantic comedies. Some of her notable works include:\n   - *The Love That Split the World* (2016)\n   - *A Million Junes* (2017)\n   - *Beach Read* (2020)\n   - *People We Meet on Vacation* (2021)\n   - *Book Lovers* (2022)\n   - *Happy Place* (2023)\n   - *Funny Story* (2024, upcoming)\n\n   *People We Meet on Vacation* fits into her career as a hallmark of her growth as a writer, showcasing her ability to blend humor with deeper emotional narratives effectively, solidifying her position in the contemporary romance genre.\n\n### Additional Resources\n- For a detailed look into the book, you can check the [Wikipedia page](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People_We_Meet_on_Vacation) and read critical reviews on [Open Books](https://openbooks.net/reviews/people-we-meet-on-vacation).\n- More about Emily Henry can be explored on her [author page](https://openbooks.net/authors/emily-henry) and her works are listed [here](https://openbooks.net/authors/emily-henry/works).",
      "mediaUrl": null
